1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"phase-2","kind":"phase-index","route":"/roadmap/phase-2","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/phase-2","sourceHash":"000aa9cd61e715db177704744992321e6340b1c9f6715b0aa988ff5f6982fb37","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T23:11:42.179Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"Comprehension","zh":"理解能力"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"segment-0001","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Phase 2 is where your language learning really starts to accelerate. Your goal is to build strong comprehension and the ability to understand real content made for native speakers by combining vocabulary growth with massive amounts of reading alongside audio.","zh":"第二阶段是你的语言学习真正开始加速的阶段。你的目标是通过词汇增长，以及大量结合音频的阅读，建立强大的理解能力，并能够理解面向母语者制作的真实内容。"}},{"id":"segment-0002","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"You'll be reading for most of this phase, but not in the way you might expect. \"Reading\" here doesn't just mean books. It means anything with text: TV shows with subtitles, YouTube videos, comics, blogs, articles. You'll almost always be reading <em>with</em> audio playing simultaneously, which keeps your ears developing even as your reading ability pulls ahead. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/reading-doesn-t-mean-books\">Reading Doesn't Mean Books</a>","zh":"这一阶段的大部分时间你都会进行阅读，但方式可能和你想象的不一样。这里的“阅读”不只是读书，而是指任何包含文字的内容：带字幕的电视剧、YouTube 视频、漫画、博客、文章。你几乎总会<em>同时配合</em>播放音频，这样即使阅读能力领先，听力也能持续发展。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/reading-doesn-t-mean-books\">阅读不等于读书</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0003","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"This approach — leading with reading — is deliberate. Reading is much easier than listening because you control the pace. You can pause, reread, and look things up. This lets you build a large base of comprehension faster than listening alone would allow. Your listening will catch up in Phase 3, and because you'll already know so many words and patterns, it will catch up quickly. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-reading-listening-gap\">The Reading-Listening Gap</a>","zh":"这种以阅读为主导的方法是经过刻意设计的。阅读比听力容易得多，因为你可以控制节奏。你可以暂停、重读和查词。这能让你比单靠听力更快地建立庞大的理解基础。你的听力会在第三阶段追上来，而且由于你已经掌握了大量词汇和规律，追赶速度会很快。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-reading-listening-gap\">阅读与听力的差距</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0004","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"By the end of Phase 2, you'll be able to read subtitles and follow and enjoy a TV show made for adults with the help of tools.","zh":"到第二阶段结束时，借助工具，你将能够阅读字幕、跟上并享受一部面向成年观众制作的电视剧。"}},{"id":"hour-estimates","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Hour Estimates","zh":"时间估算"}},{"id":"segment-0006","type":"table","rows":[[{"en":"","zh":"","header":true},{"en":"Cousin","zh":"近亲语言","header":true},{"en":"Similar","zh":"相近语言","header":true},{"en":"Neutral","zh":"中性","header":true},{"en":"Distant","zh":"远亲语言","header":true}],[{"en":"This phase","zh":"本阶段","header":false},{"en":"180","zh":"180","header":false},{"en":"375","zh":"375","header":false},{"en":"400","zh":"400","header":false},{"en":"600","zh":"600","header":false}],[{"en":"Cumulative","zh":"累计","header":false},{"en":"220","zh":"220","header":false},{"en":"450","zh":"450","header":false},{"en":"500","zh":"500","header":false},{"en":"750","zh":"750","header":false}]]},{"id":"sub-phases","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Sub-phases","zh":"子阶段"}},{"id":"segment-0008","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>2A — Learn the Core Words:</strong> Expand your vocabulary to the 2000 most common words, which form the core of any language. With these words, you'll understand the backbone of most sentences.","zh":"<strong>2A——学习核心词汇：</strong>将词汇量扩展到最常见的2000个词，它们构成任何语言的核心。掌握这些词后，你将理解大多数句子的骨架。"}},{"id":"segment-0009","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>2B — Develop Your Comprehension:</strong> Move beyond common words and into domain-specific vocabulary using sentence mining. This is where you start truly enjoying native content.","zh":"<strong>2B——发展理解能力：</strong>通过句子挖掘，从常见词汇进一步进入领域特定词汇。此时，你将开始真正享受母语内容。"}},{"id":"segment-0010","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>2C — Solidify Your Reading:</strong> Shift the balance from interactive to freeflow immersion. By the end, you'll read comfortably without tools.","zh":"<strong>2C——巩固阅读能力：</strong>将学习重点从互动沉浸转向自由流沉浸。到最后，你将能够不借助工具自在地阅读。"}}],"cards":[{"href":"/roadmap/phase-2/2a-learn-the-core-words","title":{"en":"2ALearn the Core Words","zh":"2A学习核心词汇"}},{"href":"/roadmap/phase-2/2b-develop-your-comprehension","title":{"en":"2BDevelop your Comprehension","zh":"2B发展理解能力"}},{"href":"/roadmap/phase-2/2c-solidify-your-reading","title":{"en":"2CSolidify your Reading","zh":"2C巩固阅读能力"}}]}}]
